  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The title page is signed and dated by Brian Routh with the copyright date 1976. All illustrated leaves are signed by Brian Routh in the lower right corner on the recto.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The front cover has a hand-painted cover title and illustration and is signed by hand in the lower right: The Kipper Kids H. Kipper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="545" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Brian Routh is a performance/sound artist from the United Kingdom. He is known for his performance work with Martin von Haselberg as one of The Kipper Kids who became notorious for their rowdy and rebellious performances in the art world; influencing, among others, the punk movement. The Kipper Kids performed throughout Europe, North Africa, United Kingdom, North America and Canada. They also worked on a number of projects for HBO and Cinemax as well as cameos in various movies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1="2" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">This unique hand-painted book by Brian Routh, a.k.a. Harry Kipper of the performance art duo The Kipper Kids, is executed in a comic book style and depicts the Kipper Kids and the elements of their performance artworks within a fantastical setting that spans oceans, time periods, and multiple types of storytelling.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="563" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in heavy weight construction paper folded vertically and secured with a black cloth ribbon.</subfield>
